          },
          {
            "id": 598,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-N8VPdDnevo7Yqdx9uL5l1kUNgSx\">Looking at cities with higher water reserves, Sydney and Canberra both recorded figures of approximately 75% in 2009, whereas Brisbane's reservoirs were about 55% full. By 2010, despite Brisbane's water level remaining stable, Sydney saw a modest increase to 81%, and Canberra experienced a substantial rise to 98% of its maximum volume.</div>\n</div>",
