            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-K4H9d92tPonK9Qx9yhzltkubgYb\">Regarding the remaining cities, Darwin and Perth had relatively similar water levels in 2009, at around 44% and 40% respectively, while Melbourne had the lowest initial level at 25%. In contrast to Perth's level rising significantly to 61% in the following year, Darwin's figure fell to approximately 28%. Meanwhile, Melbourne saw its water level increase considerably to 38% by the end of the period.</div>\n</div>",
